        "flex-wrap\u{1}Controls whether the flex container is single-line or multi-line, and the direction of the cross-axis, which determines the direction new lines are stacked in.\u{1}nowrap wrap wrap-reverse\u{1}nowrap | wrap | wrap-reverse\u{1}",
        "float\u{1}Specifies how a box should be floated. It may be set for any element, but only applies to elements that generate boxes that are not absolutely positioned.\u{1}inline-end inline-start left none right\u{1}left | right | none | inline-start | inline-end\u{1}",
        "flood-color\u{1}Indicates what color to use to flood the current filter primitive subregion.\u{1}\u{1}<color>\u{1}",
        "flood-opacity\u{1}Indicates what opacity to use to flood the current filter primitive subregion.\u{1}\u{1}<'opacity'>\u{1}",
        "font\u{1}Shorthand property for setting 'font-style', 'font-variant', 'font-weight', 'font-size', 'line-height', and 'font-family', at the same place in the style sheet.\u{1}100 200 300 400 500 600 700 800 900 bold bolder caption icon italic large larger lighter medium menu message-box normal oblique small small-caps small-caption smaller status-bar x-large x-small xx-large xx-small\u{1}[ [ <'font-style'> || <font-variant-css2> || <'font-weight'> || <font-width-css3> ]? <'font-size'> [ / <'line-height'> ]\u{1}",
        "font-family\u{1}Specifies a prioritized list of font family names or generic family names. A user agent iterates through the list of family names until it matches an available font that contains a glyph for the character to be rendered.\u{1}cursive fantasy monospace sans-serif serif\u{1}<family-name>#\u{1}",
        "font-feature-settings\u{1}Provides low-level control over OpenType font features. It is intended as a way of providing access to font features that are not widely used but are needed for a particular use case.\u{1}\"aalt\" \"abvf\" \"abvm\" \"abvs\" \"afrc\" \"akhn\" \"blwf\" \"blwm\" \"blws\" \"calt\" \"case\" \"ccmp\" \"cfar\" \"cjct\" \"clig\" \"cpct\" \"cpsp\" \"cswh\" \"curs\" \"c2pc\" \"c2sc\" \"dist\" \"dlig\" \"dnom\" \"dtls\" \"expt\" \"falt\" \"fin2\" \"fin3\" \"fina\" \"flac\" \"frac\" \"fwid\" \"half\" \"haln\" \"halt\" \"hist\" \"hkna\" \"hlig\" \"hngl\" \"hojo\" \"hwid\" \"init\" \"isol\" \"ital\" \"jalt\" \"jp78\" \"jp83\" \"jp90\" \"jp04\" \"kern\" \"lfbd\" \"liga\" \"ljmo\" \"lnum\" \"locl\" \"ltra\" \"ltrm\" \"mark\" \"med2\" \"medi\" \"mgrk\" \"mkmk\" \"nalt\" \"nlck\" \"nukt\" \"numr\" \"onum\" \"opbd\" \"ordn\" \"ornm\" \"palt\" \"pcap\" \"pkna\" \"pnum\" \"pref\" \"pres\" \"pstf\" \"psts\" \"pwid\" \"qwid\" \"rand\" \"rclt\" \"rlig\" \"rkrf\" \"rphf\" \"rtbd\" \"rtla\" \"rtlm\" \"ruby\" \"salt\" \"sinf\" \"size\" \"smcp\" \"smpl\" \"ssty\" \"stch\" \"subs\" \"sups\" \"swsh\" \"titl\" \"tjmo\" \"tnam\" \"tnum\" \"trad\" \"twid\" \"unic\" \"valt\" \"vatu\" \"vert\" \"vhal\" \"vjmo\" \"vkna\" \"vkrn\" \"vpal\" \"vrt2\" \"zero\" normal off on\u{1}normal | <feature-tag-value>#\u{1}",
        "font-kerning\u{1}Kerning is the contextual adjustment of inter-glyph spacing. This property controls metric kerning, kerning that utilizes adjustment data contained in the font.\u{1}auto none normal\u{1}auto | normal | none\u{1}",
        "font-language-override\u{1}The value of 'normal' implies that when rendering with OpenType fonts the language of the document is used to infer the OpenType language system, used to select language specific features when rendering.\u{1}normal\u{1}normal | <string>\u{1}",
        "font-size\u{1}Indicates the desired height of glyphs from the font. For scalable fonts, the font-size is a scale factor applied to the EM unit of the font.\u{1}large larger medium small smaller x-large x-small xx-large xx-small\u{1}<absolute-size> | <relative-size> | <length-percentage [0,\u{221e}]> | math\u{1}",
        "font-size-adjust\u{1}Preserves the readability of text when font fallback occurs by adjusting the font-size so that the x-height is the same regardless of the font used.\u{1}none\u{1}none | [ ex-height | cap-height | ch-width | ic-width | ic-height ]? [ from-font | <number> ]\u{1}",
        "font-stretch\u{1}Selects a normal, condensed, or expanded face from a font family.\u{1}condensed expanded extra-condensed extra-expanded narrower normal semi-condensed semi-expanded ultra-condensed ultra-expanded wider\u{1}<font-stretch-absolute>{1,2}\u{1}x",
        "font-style\u{1}Allows italic or oblique faces to be selected. Italic forms are generally cursive in nature while oblique faces are typically sloped versions of the regular face.\u{1}italic normal oblique\u{1}normal | italic | oblique <angle>{0,2}\u{1}",
        "font-synthesis\u{1}Controls whether user agents are allowed to synthesize bold or oblique font faces when a font family lacks bold or italic faces.\u{1}none style weight\u{1}none | [ weight || style || small-caps || position]\u{1}",
        "font-variant\u{1}Specifies variant representations of the font\u{1}normal small-caps\u{1}normal | none | [ <common-lig-values> || <discretionary-lig-values> || <historical-lig-values> || <contextual-alt-values\u{1}",
        "font-variant-alternates\u{1}For any given character, fonts can provide a variety of alternate glyphs in addition to the default glyph for that character. This property provides control over the selection of these alternate glyphs.\u{1}annotation() character-variant() historical-forms normal ornaments() styleset() stylistic() swash()\u{1}normal | [ stylistic( <feature-value-name> ) || historical-forms || styleset( <feature-value-name># ) || character-varia\u{1}",
        "font-variant-caps\u{1}Specifies control over capitalized forms.\u{1}all-petite-caps all-small-caps normal petite-caps small-caps titling-caps unicase\u{1}normal | small-caps | all-small-caps | petite-caps | all-petite-caps | unicase | titling-caps\u{1}",
        "font-variant-east-asian\u{1}Allows control of glyph substitute and positioning in East Asian text.\u{1}full-width jis04 jis78 jis83 jis90 normal proportional-width ruby simplified traditional\u{1}normal | [ <east-asian-variant-values> || <east-asian-width-values> || ruby ]\u{1}",
        "font-variant-ligatures\u{1}Specifies control over which ligatures are enabled or disabled. A value of 'normal' implies that the defaults set by the font are used.\u{1}additional-ligatures common-ligatures contextual discretionary-ligatures historical-ligatures no-additional-ligatures no-common-ligatures no-contextual no-discretionary-ligatures no-historical-ligatures none normal\u{1}normal | none | [ <common-lig-values> || <discretionary-lig-values> || <historical-lig-values> || <contextual-alt-values\u{1}",
        "font-variant-numeric\u{1}Specifies control over numerical forms.\u{1}diagonal-fractions lining-nums normal oldstyle-nums ordinal proportional-nums slashed-zero stacked-fractions tabular-nums\u{1}normal | [ <numeric-figure-values> || <numeric-spacing-values> || <numeric-fraction-values> || ordinal || slashed-zero ]\u{1}",
        "font-variant-position\u{1}Specifies the vertical position\u{1}normal sub super\u{1}normal | sub | super\u{1}",
        "font-weight\u{1}Specifies weight of glyphs in the font, their degree of blackness or stroke thickness.\u{1}100 200 300 400 500 600 700 800 900 bold bolder lighter normal\u{1}<font-weight-absolute>{1,2}\u{1}",
        "glyph-orientation-horizontal\u{1}Controls glyph orientation when the inline-progression-direction is horizontal.\u{1}\u{1}\u{1}",
        "glyph-orientation-vertical\u{1}Controls glyph orientation when the inline-progression-direction is vertical.\u{1}auto\u{1}\u{1}",
        "grid-area\u{1}Determine a grid item's size and location within the grid by contributing a line, a span, or nothing (automatic) to its grid placement. Shorthand for 'grid-row-start', 'grid-column-start', 'grid-row-end', and 'grid-column-end'.\u{1}auto span\u{1}<grid-line> [ / <grid-line> ]{0,3}\u{1}",
        "grid\u{1}The grid CSS property is a shorthand property that sets all of the explicit grid properties ('grid-template-rows', 'grid-template-columns', and 'grid-template-areas'), and all the implicit grid properties ('grid-auto-rows',...\u{1}\u{1}<'grid-template'> | <'grid-template-rows'> / [ auto-flow && dense? ] <'grid-auto-columns'>? | [ auto-flow && dense? ] <'\u{1}",
        "grid-auto-columns\u{1}Specifies the size of implicitly created columns.\u{1}min-content max-content auto minmax()\u{1}<track-size>+\u{1}",
        "grid-auto-flow\u{1}Controls how the auto-placement algorithm works, specifying exactly how auto-placed items get flowed into the grid.\u{1}row column dense\u{1}[ row | column ] || dense\u{1}",
        "grid-auto-rows\u{1}Specifies the size of implicitly created rows.\u{1}min-content max-content auto minmax()\u{1}<track-size>+\u{1}",
        "grid-column\u{1}Shorthand for 'grid-column-start' and 'grid-column-end'.\u{1}auto span\u{1}<grid-line> [ / <grid-line> ]?\u{1}",
        "grid-column-end\u{1}Determine a grid item's size and location within the grid by contributing a line, a span, or nothing (automatic) to its grid placement.\u{1}auto span\u{1}<grid-line>\u{1}",
        "grid-column-gap\u{1}Specifies the gutters between grid columns. Replaced by 'column-gap' property.\u{1}\u{1}<length-percentage>\u{1}x",
        "grid-column-start\u{1}Determine a grid item's size and location within the grid by contributing a line, a span, or nothing (automatic) to its grid placement.\u{1}auto span\u{1}<grid-line>\u{1}",
        "grid-gap\u{1}Shorthand that specifies the gutters between grid columns and grid rows in one declaration. Replaced by 'gap' property.\u{1}\u{1}<'grid-row-gap'> <'grid-column-gap'>?\u{1}x",
        "grid-row\u{1}Shorthand for 'grid-row-start' and 'grid-row-end'.\u{1}auto span\u{1}<grid-line> [ / <grid-line> ]?\u{1}",
        "grid-row-end\u{1}Determine a grid item's size and location within the grid by contributing a line, a span, or nothing (automatic) to its grid placement.\u{1}auto span\u{1}<grid-line>\u{1}",
        "grid-row-gap\u{1}Specifies the gutters between grid rows. Replaced by 'row-gap' property.\u{1}\u{1}<length-percentage>\u{1}x",
        "grid-row-start\u{1}Determine a grid item's size and location within the grid by contributing a line, a span, or nothing (automatic) to its grid placement.\u{1}auto span\u{1}<grid-line>\u{1}",
        "grid-template\u{1}Shorthand for setting grid-template-columns, grid-template-rows, and grid-template-areas in a single declaration.\u{1}none min-content max-content auto subgrid minmax() repeat()\u{1}none | [ <'grid-template-rows'> / <'grid-template-columns'> ] | [ <line-names>? <string> <track-size>? <line-names>? ]+ \u{1}",
        "grid-template-areas\u{1}Specifies named grid areas, which are not associated with any particular grid item, but can be referenced from the grid-placement properties.\u{1}none\u{1}none | <string>+\u{1}",
        "grid-template-columns\u{1}specifies, as a space-separated track list, the line names and track sizing functions of the grid.\u{1}none min-content max-content auto subgrid minmax() repeat()\u{1}none | <track-list> | <auto-track-list> | subgrid <line-name-list>?\u{1}",
        "grid-template-rows\u{1}specifies, as a space-separated track list, the line names and track sizing functions of the grid.\u{1}none min-content max-content auto subgrid minmax() repeat()\u{1}none | <track-list> | <auto-track-list> | subgrid <line-name-list>?\u{1}",
        "height\u{1}Specifies the height of the content area, padding area or border area (depending on 'box-sizing') of certain boxes.\u{1}auto fit-content max-content min-content\u{1}auto | <length-percentage [0,\u{221e}]> | min-content | max-content | fit-content | fit-content(<length-percentage [0,\u{221e}]>) | <c\u{1}",
        "hyphens\u{1}Controls whether hyphenation is allowed to create more break opportunities within a line of text.\u{1}auto manual none\u{1}none | manual | auto\u{1}",
        "image-orientation\u{1}Specifies an orthogonal rotation to be applied to an image before it is laid out.\u{1}flip from-image\u{1}from-image | <angle> | [ <angle>? flip ]\u{1}",
        "image-rendering\u{1}Provides a hint to the user-agent about what aspects of an image are most important to preserve when the image is scaled, to aid the user-agent in the choice of an appropriate scaling algorithm.\u{1}auto crisp-edges -moz-crisp-edges optimizeQuality optimizeSpeed pixelated\u{1}auto | crisp-edges | pixelated | smooth\u{1}",
        "ime-mode\u{1}Controls the state of the input method editor for text fields.\u{1}active auto disabled inactive normal\u{1}auto | normal | active | inactive | disabled\u{1}x",
        "inline-size\u{1}Size of an element in the direction specified by 'writing-mode'.\u{1}auto\u{1}<'width'>\u{1}",
        "isolation\u{1}In CSS setting to 'isolate' will turn the element into a stacking context. In SVG, it defines whether an element is isolated or not.\u{1}auto isolate\u{1}auto | isolate\u{1}",
        "justify-content\u{1}Aligns flex items along the main axis of the current line of the flex container.\u{1}center start end left right safe unsafe stretch space-evenly flex-end flex-start space-around space-between baseline\u{1}normal | <content-distribution> | <overflow-position>? [ <content-position> | left | right ]\u{1}",
        "kerning\u{1}Indicates whether the user agent should adjust inter-glyph spacing based on kerning tables that are included in the relevant font or instead disable auto-kerning and set inter-character spacing to a specific length.\u{1}auto\u{1}\u{1}",
        "left\u{1}Specifies how far an absolutely positioned box's left margin edge is offset to the right of the left edge of the box's 'containing block'.\u{1}auto\u{1}auto | <length-percentage> | <anchor()> | <anchor-size()>\u{1}",
        "letter-spacing\u{1}Specifies the minimum, maximum, and optimal spacing between grapheme clusters.\u{1}normal\u{1}normal | <length>\u{1}",
        "lighting-color\u{1}Defines the color of the light source for filter primitives 'feDiffuseLighting' and 'feSpecularLighting'.\u{1}\u{1}<color>\u{1}",
        "line-break\u{1}Specifies what set of line breaking restrictions are in effect within the element.\u{1}auto loose normal strict anywhere\u{1}auto | loose | normal | strict | anywhere\u{1}",
        "line-height\u{1}Determines the block-progression dimension of the text content area of an inline box.\u{1}normal\u{1}normal | <number> | <length> | <percentage>\u{1}",
        "list-style\u{1}Shorthand for setting 'list-style-type', 'list-style-position' and 'list-style-image'\u{1}armenian circle decimal decimal-leading-zero disc georgian inside lower-alpha lower-greek lower-latin lower-roman none outside square symbols() upper-alpha upper-latin upper-roman url()\u{1}<'list-style-type'> || <'list-style-position'> || <'list-style-image'>\u{1}",
        "list-style-image\u{1}Sets the image that will be used as the list item marker. When the image is available, it will replace the marker set with the 'list-style-type' marker.\u{1}none\u{1}<image> | none\u{1}",
        "list-style-position\u{1}Specifies the position of the '::marker' pseudo-element's box in the list item.\u{1}inside outside\u{1}inside | outside\u{1}",
        "list-style-type\u{1}Used to construct the default contents of a list item's marker\u{1}armenian circle decimal decimal-leading-zero disc georgian lower-alpha lower-greek lower-latin lower-roman none square symbols() upper-alpha upper-latin upper-roman\u{1}<counter-style> | <string> | none\u{1}",
        "margin\u{1}Shorthand property to set values for the thickness of the margin area. If left is omitted, it is the same as right. If bottom is omitted it is the same as top, if right is omitted it is the same as top.\u{1}auto\u{1}<'margin-top'>{1,4}\u{1}",
        "margin-block-end\u{1}Logical 'margin-bottom'. Mapping depends on the parent element's 'writing-mode', 'direction', and 'text-orientation'.\u{1}auto\u{1}<'margin-top'>\u{1}",
        "margin-block-start\u{1}Logical 'margin-top'. Mapping depends on the parent element's 'writing-mode', 'direction', and 'text-orientation'.\u{1}auto\u{1}<'margin-top'>\u{1}",
        "margin-bottom\u{1}Shorthand property to set values for the thickness of the margin area. If left is omitted, it is the same as right. If bottom is omitted it is the same as top, if right is omitted it is the same as top.\u{1}auto\u{1}<length-percentage> | auto | <anchor-size()>\u{1}",
        "margin-inline-end\u{1}Logical 'margin-right'. Mapping depends on the parent element's 'writing-mode', 'direction', and 'text-orientation'.\u{1}auto\u{1}<'margin-top'>\u{1}",
        "margin-inline-start\u{1}Logical 'margin-left'. Mapping depends on the parent element's 'writing-mode', 'direction', and 'text-orientation'.\u{1}auto\u{1}<'margin-top'>\u{1}",
        "margin-left\u{1}Shorthand property to set values for the thickness of the margin area. If left is omitted, it is the same as right. If bottom is omitted it is the same as top, if right is omitted it is the same as top.\u{1}auto\u{1}<length-percentage> | auto | <anchor-size()>\u{1}",
        "margin-right\u{1}Shorthand property to set values for the thickness of the margin area. If left is omitted, it is the same as right. If bottom is omitted it is the same as top, if right is omitted it is the same as top.\u{1}auto\u{1}<length-percentage> | auto | <anchor-size()>\u{1}",
        "margin-top\u{1}Shorthand property to set values for the thickness of the margin area. If left is omitted, it is the same as right. If bottom is omitted it is the same as top, if right is omitted it is the same as top.\u{1}auto\u{1}<length-percentage> | auto | <anchor-size()>\u{1}",
        "marker\u{1}Specifies the marker symbol that shall be used for all points on the sets the value for all vertices on the given 'path' element or basic shape.\u{1}none url()\u{1}none | <url>\u{1}",
        "marker-end\u{1}Specifies the marker that will be drawn at the last vertices of the given markable element.\u{1}none url()\u{1}none | <url>\u{1}",
        "marker-mid\u{1}Specifies the marker that will be drawn at all vertices except the first and last.\u{1}none url()\u{1}none | <url>\u{1}",
        "marker-start\u{1}Specifies the marker that will be drawn at the first vertices of the given markable element.\u{1}none url()\u{1}none | <url>\u{1}",
        "mask-image\u{1}Sets the mask layer image of an element.\u{1}none url()\u{1}<mask-reference>#\u{1}",
        "mask-mode\u{1}Indicates whether the mask layer image is treated as luminance mask or alpha mask.\u{1}alpha auto luminance\u{1}<masking-mode>#\u{1}",
        "mask-origin\u{1}Specifies the mask positioning area.\u{1}\u{1}<coord-box>#\u{1}",
        "mask-position\u{1}Specifies how mask layer images are positioned.\u{1}\u{1}<position>#\u{1}",
        "mask-repeat\u{1}Specifies how mask layer images are tiled after they have been sized and positioned.\u{1}\u{1}<repeat-style>#\u{1}",
        "mask-size\u{1}Specifies the size of the mask layer images.\u{1}auto contain cover\u{1}<bg-size>#\u{1}",
        "mask-type\u{1}Defines whether the content of the <mask> element is treated as as luminance mask or alpha mask.\u{1}alpha luminance\u{1}luminance | alpha\u{1}",
        "max-block-size\u{1}Maximum size of an element in the direction opposite that of the direction specified by 'writing-mode'.\u{1}none\u{1}<'max-width'>\u{1}",
        "max-height\u{1}Allows authors to constrain content height to a certain range.\u{1}none fit-content max-content min-content\u{1}none | <length-percentage [0,\u{221e}]> | min-content | max-content | fit-content | fit-content(<length-percentage [0,\u{221e}]>) | <c\u{1}",
        "max-inline-size\u{1}Maximum size of an element in the direction specified by 'writing-mode'.\u{1}none\u{1}<'max-width'>\u{1}",
        "max-width\u{1}Allows authors to constrain content width to a certain range.\u{1}none fit-content max-content min-content\u{1}none | <length-percentage [0,\u{221e}]> | min-content | max-content | fit-content | fit-content(<length-percentage [0,\u{221e}]>) | <c\u{1}",
        "min-block-size\u{1}Minimal size of an element in the direction opposite that of the direction specified by 'writing-mode'.\u{1}\u{1}<'min-width'>\u{1}",
        "min-height\u{1}Allows authors to constrain content height to a certain range.\u{1}auto fit-content max-content min-content\u{1}auto | <length-percentage [0,\u{221e}]> | min-content | max-content | fit-content | fit-content(<length-percentage [0,\u{221e}]>) | <c\u{1}",
        "min-inline-size\u{1}Minimal size of an element in the direction specified by 'writing-mode'.\u{1}\u{1}<'min-width'>\u{1}",
        "min-width\u{1}Allows authors to constrain content width to a certain range.\u{1}auto fit-content max-content min-content\u{1}auto | <length-percentage [0,\u{221e}]> | min-content | max-content | fit-content | fit-content(<length-percentage [0,\u{221e}]>) | <c\u{1}",
        "mix-blend-mode\u{1}Defines the formula that must be used to mix the colors with the backdrop.\u{1}normal multiply screen overlay darken lighten color-dodge color-burn hard-light soft-light difference exclusion hue saturation color luminosity\u{1}<blend-mode> | plus-darker | plus-lighter\u{1}",
        "motion\u{1}Shorthand property for setting 'motion-path', 'motion-offset' and 'motion-rotation'.\u{1}none path() auto reverse\u{1}\u{1}",
        "motion-offset\u{1}A distance that describes the position along the specified motion path.\u{1}\u{1}\u{1}",
        "motion-path\u{1}Specifies the motion path the element gets positioned at.\u{1}none path()\u{1}\u{1}",
        "motion-rotation\u{1}Defines the direction of the element while positioning along the motion path.\u{1}auto reverse\u{1}\u{1}",
        "-moz-appearance\u{1}Used in Gecko (Firefox) to display an element using a platform-native styling based on the operating system's theme.\u{1}button button-arrow-down button-arrow-next button-arrow-previous button-arrow-up button-bevel checkbox checkbox-container checkbox-label dialog groupbox listbox menuarrow menuimage menuitem menuitemtext menulist menulist-button menulist-text menulist-textfield menupopup menuradio menuseparator -moz-mac-unified-toolbar -moz-win-borderless-glass -moz-win-browsertabbar-toolbox -moz-win-communications-toolbox -moz-win-glass -moz-win-media-toolbox none progressbar progresschunk radio radio-container radio-label radiomenuitem resizer resizerpanel scrollbarbutton-down scrollbarbutton-left scrollbarbutton-right scrollbarbutton-up scrollbar-small scrollbartrack-horizontal scrollbartrack-vertical separator spinner spinner-downbutton spinner-textfield spinner-upbutton statusbar statusbarpanel tab tabpanels tab-scroll-arrow-back tab-scroll-arrow-forward textfield textfield-multiline toolbar toolbox tooltip treeheadercell treeheadersortarrow treeitem treetwistyopen treeview treewisty window\u{1}none | button | button-arrow-down | button-arrow-next | button-arrow-previous | button-arrow-up | button-bevel | button-\u{1}x",
