        "page-break-after\u{1}Defines rules for page breaks after an element.\u{1}always auto avoid left right\u{1}auto | always | avoid | left | right | recto | verso\u{1}x",
        "page-break-before\u{1}Defines rules for page breaks before an element.\u{1}always auto avoid left right\u{1}auto | always | avoid | left | right | recto | verso\u{1}x",
        "page-break-inside\u{1}Defines rules for page breaks inside an element.\u{1}auto avoid\u{1}auto | avoid\u{1}x",
        "paint-order\u{1}Controls the order that the three paint operations that shapes and text are rendered with: their fill, their stroke and any markers they might have.\u{1}fill markers normal stroke\u{1}normal | [ fill || stroke || markers ]\u{1}",
        "perspective\u{1}Applies the same transform as the perspective(<number>) transform function, except that it applies only to the positioned or transformed children of the element, not to the transform on the element itself.\u{1}none\u{1}none | <length>\u{1}",
        "perspective-origin\u{1}Establishes the origin for the perspective property. It effectively sets the X and Y position at which the viewer appears to be looking at the children of the element.\u{1}\u{1}<position>\u{1}",
        "pointer-events\u{1}Specifies under what circumstances a given element can be the target element for a pointer event.\u{1}all fill none painted stroke visible visibleFill visiblePainted visibleStroke\u{1}auto | none | visiblePainted | visibleFill | visibleStroke | visible | painted | fill | stroke | all | inherit\u{1}",
        "position\u{1}The position CSS property sets how an element is positioned in a document. The top, right, bottom, and left properties determine the final location of positioned elements.\u{1}absolute fixed -ms-page relative static sticky -webkit-sticky\u{1}static | relative | absolute | sticky | fixed\u{1}",
        "prefix\u{1}@counter-style descriptor. Specifies a <symbol> that is prepended to the marker representation.\u{1}\u{1}<symbol>\u{1}",
        "quotes\u{1}Specifies quotation marks for any number of embedded quotations.\u{1}none\u{1}none | auto | [ <string> <string> ]+\u{1}",
        "range\u{1}@counter-style descriptor. Defines the ranges over which the counter style is defined.\u{1}auto infinite\u{1}[ [ <integer> | infinite ]{2} ]# | auto\u{1}",
        "resize\u{1}Specifies whether or not an element is resizable by the user, and if so, along which axis/axes.\u{1}both horizontal none vertical\u{1}none | both | horizontal | vertical | block | inline\u{1}",
        "right\u{1}Specifies how far an absolutely positioned box's right margin edge is offset to the left of the right edge of the box's 'containing block'.\u{1}auto\u{1}auto | <length-percentage> | <anchor()> | <anchor-size()>\u{1}",
        "ruby-align\u{1}Specifies how text is distributed within the various ruby boxes when their contents do not exactly fill their respective boxes.\u{1}auto center distribute-letter distribute-space left line-edge right start space-between space-around\u{1}start | center | space-between | space-around\u{1}",
        "ruby-overhang\u{1}Determines whether, and on which side, ruby text is allowed to partially overhang any adjacent text in addition to its own base, when the ruby text is wider than the ruby base.\u{1}auto end none start\u{1}auto | none\u{1}",
        "ruby-position\u{1}Used by the parent of elements with display: ruby-text to control the position of the ruby text with respect to its base.\u{1}after before inline right\u{1}[ alternate || [ over | under ] ] | inter-character\u{1}",
        "ruby-span\u{1}Determines whether, and on which side, ruby text is allowed to partially overhang any adjacent text in addition to its own base, when the ruby text is wider than the ruby base.\u{1}attr(x) none\u{1}\u{1}",
        "scrollbar-3dlight-color\u{1}Determines the color of the top and left edges of the scroll box and scroll arrows of a scroll bar.\u{1}\u{1}\u{1}",
        "scrollbar-arrow-color\u{1}Determines the color of the arrow elements of a scroll arrow.\u{1}\u{1}\u{1}",
        "scrollbar-base-color\u{1}Determines the color of the main elements of a scroll bar, which include the scroll box, track, and scroll arrows.\u{1}\u{1}\u{1}",
        "scrollbar-darkshadow-color\u{1}Determines the color of the gutter of a scroll bar.\u{1}\u{1}\u{1}",
        "scrollbar-face-color\u{1}Determines the color of the scroll box and scroll arrows of a scroll bar.\u{1}\u{1}\u{1}",
        "scrollbar-highlight-color\u{1}Determines the color of the top and left edges of the scroll box and scroll arrows of a scroll bar.\u{1}\u{1}\u{1}",
        "scrollbar-shadow-color\u{1}Determines the color of the bottom and right edges of the scroll box and scroll arrows of a scroll bar.\u{1}\u{1}\u{1}",
        "scrollbar-track-color\u{1}Determines the color of the track element of a scroll bar.\u{1}\u{1}\u{1}",
        "scroll-behavior\u{1}Specifies the scrolling behavior for a scrolling box, when scrolling happens due to navigation or CSSOM scrolling APIs.\u{1}auto smooth\u{1}auto | smooth\u{1}",
        "scroll-snap-coordinate\u{1}Defines the x and y coordinate within the element which will align with the nearest ancestor scroll container's snap-destination for the respective axis.\u{1}none\u{1}none | <position>#\u{1}x",
        "scroll-snap-destination\u{1}Define the x and y coordinate within the scroll container's visual viewport which element snap points will align with.\u{1}\u{1}<position>\u{1}x",
        "scroll-snap-points-x\u{1}Defines the positioning of snap points along the x axis of the scroll container it is applied to.\u{1}none repeat()\u{1}none | repeat( <length-percentage> )\u{1}x",
        "scroll-snap-points-y\u{1}Defines the positioning of snap points along the y axis of the scroll container it is applied to.\u{1}none repeat()\u{1}none | repeat( <length-percentage> )\u{1}x",
        "scroll-snap-type\u{1}Defines how strictly snap points are enforced on the scroll container.\u{1}none mandatory proximity\u{1}none | [ x | y | block | inline | both ] [ mandatory | proximity ]?\u{1}",
        "shape-image-threshold\u{1}Defines the alpha channel threshold used to extract the shape using an image. A value of 0.5 means that the shape will enclose all the pixels that are more than 50% opaque.\u{1}\u{1}<opacity-value>\u{1}",
        "shape-margin\u{1}Adds a margin to a 'shape-outside'. This defines a new shape that is the smallest contour that includes all the points that are the 'shape-margin' distance outward in the perpendicular direction from a point on the underlying...\u{1}\u{1}<length-percentage>\u{1}",
        "shape-outside\u{1}Specifies an orthogonal rotation to be applied to an image before it is laid out.\u{1}margin-box none\u{1}none | [ <shape-box> || <basic-shape> ] | <image>\u{1}",
        "shape-rendering\u{1}Provides hints about what tradeoffs to make as it renders vector graphics elements such as <path> elements and basic shapes such as circles and rectangles.\u{1}auto crispEdges geometricPrecision optimizeSpeed\u{1}auto | optimizeSpeed | crispEdges | geometricPrecision\u{1}",
        "size\u{1}The size CSS at-rule descriptor, used with the @page at-rule, defines the size and orientation of the box which is used to represent a page.\u{1}\u{1}<length [0,\u{221e}]>{1,2} | auto | [ <page-size> || [ portrait | landscape ] ]\u{1}",
        "src\u{1}@font-face descriptor. Specifies the resource containing font data. It is required, whether the font is downloadable or locally installed.\u{1}url() format() local()\u{1}[ <url> [ format( <string># ) ]? | local( <family-name> ) ]#\u{1}",
        "stop-color\u{1}Indicates what color to use at that gradient stop.\u{1}\u{1}<'color'>\u{1}",
        "stop-opacity\u{1}Defines the opacity of a given gradient stop.\u{1}\u{1}<'opacity'>\u{1}",
        "stroke\u{1}Paints along the outline of the given graphical element.\u{1}url() none\u{1}<paint>\u{1}",
        "stroke-dasharray\u{1}Controls the pattern of dashes and gaps used to stroke paths.\u{1}none\u{1}none | <dasharray>\u{1}",
        "stroke-dashoffset\u{1}Specifies the distance into the dash pattern to start the dash.\u{1}\u{1}<length-percentage> | <number>\u{1}",
        "stroke-linecap\u{1}Specifies the shape to be used at the end of open subpaths when they are stroked.\u{1}butt round square\u{1}butt | round | square\u{1}",
        "stroke-linejoin\u{1}Specifies the shape to be used at the corners of paths or basic shapes when they are stroked.\u{1}bevel miter round\u{1}miter | miter-clip | round | bevel | arcs\u{1}",
        "stroke-miterlimit\u{1}When two line segments meet at a sharp angle and miter joins have been specified for 'stroke-linejoin', it is possible for the miter to extend far beyond the thickness of the line stroking the path.\u{1}\u{1}<number>\u{1}",
        "stroke-opacity\u{1}Specifies the opacity of the painting operation used to stroke the current object.\u{1}\u{1}<'opacity'>\u{1}",
        "stroke-width\u{1}Specifies the width of the stroke on the current object.\u{1}\u{1}<length-percentage> | <number>\u{1}",
        "suffix\u{1}@counter-style descriptor. Specifies a <symbol> that is appended to the marker representation.\u{1}\u{1}<symbol>\u{1}",
        "system\u{1}@counter-style descriptor. Specifies which algorithm will be used to construct the counter's representation based on the counter value.\u{1}additive alphabetic cyclic extends fixed numeric symbolic\u{1}cyclic | numeric | alphabetic | symbolic | additive | [ fixed <integer>? ] | [ extends <counter-style-name> ]\u{1}",
        "symbols\u{1}@counter-style descriptor. Specifies the symbols used by the marker-construction algorithm specified by the system descriptor.\u{1}\u{1}<symbol>+\u{1}",
        "table-layout\u{1}Controls the algorithm used to lay out the table cells, rows, and columns.\u{1}auto fixed\u{1}auto | fixed\u{1}",
        "tab-size\u{1}Determines the width of the tab character (U+0009), in space characters (U+0020), when rendered.\u{1}\u{1}<integer> | <length>\u{1}",
        "text-align\u{1}Describes how inline contents of a block are horizontally aligned if the contents do not completely fill the line box.\u{1}center end justify left right start\u{1}start | end | left | right | center | justify | match-parent\u{1}",
        "text-align-last\u{1}Describes how the last line of a block or a line right before a forced line break is aligned when 'text-align' is set to 'justify'.\u{1}auto center justify left right\u{1}auto | start | end | left | right | center | justify\u{1}",
        "text-anchor\u{1}Used to align (start-, middle- or end-alignment) a string of text relative to a given point.\u{1}end middle start\u{1}start | middle | end\u{1}",
        "text-decoration\u{1}Decorations applied to font used for an element's text.\u{1}dashed dotted double line-through none overline solid underline wavy\u{1}<'text-decoration-line'> || <'text-decoration-style'> || <'text-decoration-color'> || <'text-decoration-thickness'>\u{1}",
        "text-decoration-color\u{1}Specifies the color of text decoration (underlines overlines, and line-throughs) set on the element with text-decoration-line.\u{1}\u{1}<color>\u{1}",
        "text-decoration-line\u{1}Specifies what line decorations, if any, are added to the element.\u{1}line-through none overline underline\u{1}none | [ underline || overline || line-through || blink ] | spelling-error | grammar-error\u{1}",
        "text-decoration-style\u{1}Specifies the line style for underline, line-through and overline text decoration.\u{1}dashed dotted double none solid wavy\u{1}solid | double | dotted | dashed | wavy\u{1}",
        "text-indent\u{1}Specifies the indentation applied to lines of inline content in a block. The indentation only affects the first line of inline content in the block unless the 'hanging' keyword is specified, in which case it affects all lines...\u{1}\u{1}<length-percentage> && hanging? && each-line?\u{1}",
        "text-justify\u{1}Selects the justification algorithm used when 'text-align' is set to 'justify'. The property applies to block containers, but the UA may (but is not required to) also support it on inline elements.\u{1}auto distribute distribute-all-lines inter-cluster inter-ideograph inter-word kashida newspaper\u{1}auto | inter-character | inter-word | none\u{1}",
        "text-orientation\u{1}Specifies the orientation of text within a line.\u{1}sideways sideways-right upright\u{1}mixed | upright | sideways\u{1}",
        "text-overflow\u{1}Text can overflow for example when it is prevented from wrapping.\u{1}clip ellipsis\u{1}[ clip | ellipsis | <string> ]{1,2}\u{1}",
        "text-rendering\u{1}The creator of SVG content might want to provide a hint to the implementation about what tradeoffs to make as it renders text. The 'text-rendering' property provides these hints.\u{1}auto geometricPrecision optimizeLegibility optimizeSpeed\u{1}auto | optimizeSpeed | optimizeLegibility | geometricPrecision\u{1}",
        "text-shadow\u{1}Enables shadow effects to be applied to the text of the element.\u{1}none\u{1}none | <shadow-t>#\u{1}",
        "text-transform\u{1}Controls capitalization effects of an element's text.\u{1}capitalize lowercase none uppercase\u{1}none | [ capitalize | uppercase | lowercase ] || full-width || full-size-kana | math-auto\u{1}",
        "text-underline-position\u{1}Sets the position of an underline specified on the same element: it does not affect underlines specified by ancestor elements.\u{1}above auto below\u{1}auto | from-font | [ under || [ left | right ] ]\u{1}",
        "top\u{1}Specifies how far an absolutely positioned box's top margin edge is offset below the top edge of the box's 'containing block'.\u{1}auto\u{1}auto | <length-percentage> | <anchor()> | <anchor-size()>\u{1}",
        "touch-action\u{1}Determines whether touch input may trigger default behavior supplied by user agent.\u{1}auto cross-slide-x cross-slide-y double-tap-zoom manipulation none pan-x pan-y pinch-zoom\u{1}auto | none | [ [ pan-x | pan-left | pan-right ] || [ pan-y | pan-up | pan-down ] || pinch-zoom ] | manipulation\u{1}",
        "transform\u{1}A two-dimensional transformation is applied to an element through the 'transform' property. This property contains a list of transform functions similar to those allowed by SVG.\u{1}matrix() matrix3d() none perspective() rotate() rotate3d() rotateX('angle') rotateY('angle') rotateZ('angle') scale() scale3d() scaleX() scaleY() scaleZ() skew() skewX() skewY() translate() translate3d() translateX() translateY() translateZ()\u{1}none | <transform-list>\u{1}",
        "transform-origin\u{1}Establishes the origin of transformation for an element.\u{1}\u{1}[ <length-percentage> | left | center | right | top | bottom ] | [ [ <length-percentage> | left | center | right ] && [ \u{1}",
        "transform-style\u{1}Defines how nested elements are rendered in 3D space.\u{1}flat preserve-3d\u{1}flat | preserve-3d\u{1}",
        "transition\u{1}Shorthand property combines four of the transition properties into a single property.\u{1}all none\u{1}<single-transition>#\u{1}",
        "transition-delay\u{1}Defines when the transition will start. It allows a transition to begin execution some period of time from when it is applied.\u{1}\u{1}<time>#\u{1}",
        "transition-duration\u{1}Specifies how long the transition from the old value to the new value should take.\u{1}\u{1}<time>#\u{1}",
        "transition-property\u{1}Specifies the name of the CSS property to which the transition is applied.\u{1}all none\u{1}none | <single-transition-property>#\u{1}",
        "transition-timing-function\u{1}Describes how the intermediate values used during a transition will be calculated.\u{1}\u{1}<easing-function>#\u{1}",
        "unicode-bidi\u{1}The level of embedding with respect to the bidirectional algorithm.\u{1}bidi-override embed isolate isolate-override normal plaintext\u{1}normal | embed | isolate | bidi-override | isolate-override | plaintext\u{1}",
        "unicode-range\u{1}@font-face descriptor. Defines the set of Unicode codepoints that may be supported by the font face for which it is declared.\u{1}U+26 U+00-7F U+80-FF U+100-17F U+180-24F U+1E00-1EFF U+250-2AF U+370-3FF U+1F00-1FFF U+400-4FF U+500-52F U+530-58F U+590-5FF U+600-6FF U+750-77F U+8A0-8FF U+700-74F U+900-97F U+980-9FF U+A00-A7F U+A80-AFF U+B00-B7F U+B80-BFF U+C00-C7F U+C80-CFF U+D00-D7F U+D80-DFF U+118A0-118FF U+E00-E7F U+1A20-1AAF U+AA80-AADF U+E80-EFF U+F00-FFF U+1000-109F U+10A0-10FF U+1200-137F U+1380-139F U+2D80-2DDF U+AB00-AB2F U+1780-17FF U+1800-18AF U+1B80-1BBF U+1CC0-1CCF U+4E00-9FD5 U+3400-4DB5 U+2F00-2FDF U+2E80-2EFF U+1100-11FF U+AC00-D7AF U+3040-309F U+30A0-30FF U+A4D0-A4FF U+A000-A48F U+A490-A4CF U+2000-206F U+3000-303F U+2070-209F U+20A0-20CF U+2100-214F U+2150-218F U+2190-21FF U+2200-22FF U+2300-23FF U+E000-F8FF U+FB00-FB4F U+FB50-FDFF U+1F600-1F64F U+2600-26FF U+1F300-1F5FF U+1F900-1F9FF U+1F680-1F6FF\u{1}<unicode-range-token>#\u{1}",
        "user-select\u{1}Controls the appearance of selection.\u{1}all auto contain none text\u{1}auto | text | none | all\u{1}",
        "vertical-align\u{1}Affects the vertical positioning of the inline boxes generated by an inline-level element inside a line box.\u{1}auto baseline bottom middle sub super text-bottom text-top top -webkit-baseline-middle\u{1}baseline | sub | super | text-top | text-bottom | middle | top | bottom | <percentage> | <length>\u{1}",
        "visibility\u{1}Specifies whether the boxes generated by an element are rendered. Invisible boxes still affect layout (set the 'display' property to 'none' to suppress box generation altogether).\u{1}collapse hidden visible\u{1}visible | hidden | collapse\u{1}",
        "-webkit-animation\u{1}Shorthand property combines six of the animation properties into a single property.\u{1}alternate alternate-reverse backwards both forwards infinite none normal reverse\u{1}\u{1}",
        "-webkit-animation-delay\u{1}Defines when the animation will start.\u{1}\u{1}\u{1}",
        "-webkit-animation-direction\u{1}Defines whether or not the animation should play in reverse on alternate cycles.\u{1}alternate alternate-reverse normal reverse\u{1}\u{1}",
        "-webkit-animation-duration\u{1}Defines the length of time that an animation takes to complete one cycle.\u{1}\u{1}\u{1}",
        "-webkit-animation-fill-mode\u{1}Defines what values are applied by the animation outside the time it is executing.\u{1}backwards both forwards none\u{1}\u{1}",
        "-webkit-animation-iteration-count\u{1}Defines the number of times an animation cycle is played. The default value is one, meaning the animation will play from beginning to end once.\u{1}infinite\u{1}\u{1}",
        "-webkit-animation-name\u{1}Defines a list of animations that apply. Each name is used to select the keyframe at-rule that provides the property values for the animation.\u{1}none\u{1}\u{1}",
        "-webkit-animation-play-state\u{1}Defines whether the animation is running or paused.\u{1}paused running\u{1}\u{1}",
        "-webkit-animation-timing-function\u{1}Describes how the animation will progress over one cycle of its duration. See the 'transition-timing-function'.\u{1}\u{1}\u{1}",
        "-webkit-appearance\u{1}Changes the appearance of buttons and other controls to resemble native controls.\u{1}button button-bevel caps-lock-indicator caret checkbox default-button listbox listitem media-fullscreen-button media-mute-button media-play-button media-seek-back-button media-seek-forward-button media-slider media-sliderthumb menulist menulist-button menulist-text menulist-textfield none push-button radio scrollbarbutton-down scrollbarbutton-left scrollbarbutton-right scrollbarbutton-up scrollbargripper-horizontal scrollbargripper-vertical scrollbarthumb-horizontal scrollbarthumb-vertical scrollbartrack-horizontal scrollbartrack-vertical searchfield searchfield-cancel-button searchfield-decoration searchfield-results-button searchfield-results-decoration slider-horizontal sliderthumb-horizontal sliderthumb-vertical slider-vertical square-button textarea textfield\u{1}none | button | button-bevel | caret | checkbox | default-button | inner-spin-button | listbox | listitem | media-contro\u{1}x",
        "-webkit-backdrop-filter\u{1}Applies a filter effect where the first filter in the list takes the element's background image as the input image.\u{1}none blur() brightness() contrast() drop-shadow() grayscale() hue-rotate() invert() opacity() saturate() sepia() url()\u{1}\u{1}",
        "-webkit-backface-visibility\u{1}Determines whether or not the 'back' side of a transformed element is visible when facing the viewer. With an identity transform, the front side of an element faces the viewer.\u{1}hidden visible\u{1}\u{1}",
        "-webkit-background-clip\u{1}Determines the background painting area.\u{1}\u{1}\u{1}",
        "-webkit-background-composite\u{1}\u{1}border padding\u{1}\u{1}",
        "-webkit-background-origin\u{1}For elements rendered as a single box, specifies the background positioning area. For elements rendered as multiple boxes (e.g., inline boxes on several lines, boxes on several pages) specifies which boxes 'box-decoration-break'...\u{1}\u{1}\u{1}",
        "-webkit-border-image\u{1}Shorthand property for setting 'border-image-source', 'border-image-slice', 'border-image-width', 'border-image-outset' and 'border-image-repeat'. Omitted values are set to their initial values.\u{1}auto fill none repeat round space stretch url()\u{1}\u{1}",
        "-webkit-box-align\u{1}Specifies the alignment of nested elements within an outer flexible box element.\u{1}baseline center end start stretch\u{1}\u{1}",
        "-webkit-box-direction\u{1}In webkit applications, -webkit-box-direction specifies whether a box lays out its contents normally (from the top or left edge), or in reverse (from the bottom or right edge).\u{1}normal reverse\u{1}\u{1}",
        "-webkit-box-flex\u{1}Specifies an element's flexibility.\u{1}\u{1}\u{1}",
        "-webkit-box-flex-group\u{1}Flexible elements can be assigned to flex groups using the 'box-flex-group' property.\u{1}\u{1}\u{1}",
        "-webkit-box-ordinal-group\u{1}Indicates the ordinal group the element belongs to. Elements with a lower ordinal group are displayed before those with a higher ordinal group.\u{1}\u{1}\u{1}",
        "-webkit-box-orient\u{1}In webkit applications, -webkit-box-orient specifies whether a box lays out its contents horizontally or vertically.\u{1}block-axis horizontal inline-axis vertical\u{1}\u{1}",
        "-webkit-box-pack\u{1}Specifies alignment of child elements within the current element in the direction of orientation.\u{1}center end justify start\u{1}\u{1}",
        "-webkit-box-reflect\u{1}Defines a reflection of a border box.\u{1}above below left right\u{1}[ above | below | right | left ]? <length>? <image>?\u{1}x",
        "-webkit-box-sizing\u{1}Box Model addition in CSS3.\u{1}border-box content-box\u{1}\u{1}",
        "-webkit-break-after\u{1}Describes the page/column break behavior before the generated box.\u{1}always auto avoid avoid-column avoid-page avoid-region column left page region right\u{1}\u{1}",
        "-webkit-break-before\u{1}Describes the page/column break behavior before the generated box.\u{1}always auto avoid avoid-column avoid-page avoid-region column left page region right\u{1}\u{1}",
        "-webkit-break-inside\u{1}Describes the page/column break behavior inside the generated box.\u{1}auto avoid avoid-column avoid-page avoid-region\u{1}\u{1}",
        "-webkit-column-break-after\u{1}Describes the page/column break behavior before the generated box.\u{1}always auto avoid avoid-column avoid-page avoid-region column left page region right\u{1}\u{1}",
        "-webkit-column-break-before\u{1}Describes the page/column break behavior before the generated box.\u{1}always auto avoid avoid-column avoid-page avoid-region column left page region right\u{1}\u{1}",
        "-webkit-column-break-inside\u{1}Describes the page/column break behavior inside the generated box.\u{1}auto avoid avoid-column avoid-page avoid-region\u{1}\u{1}",
        "-webkit-column-count\u{1}Describes the optimal number of columns into which the content of the element will be flowed.\u{1}auto\u{1}\u{1}",
        "-webkit-column-gap\u{1}Sets the gap between columns. If there is a column rule between columns, it will appear in the middle of the gap.\u{1}normal\u{1}\u{1}",
        "-webkit-column-rule\u{1}This property is a shorthand for setting 'column-rule-width', 'column-rule-style', and 'column-rule-color' at the same place in the style sheet. Omitted values are set to their initial values.\u{1}\u{1}\u{1}",
        "-webkit-column-rule-color\u{1}Sets the color of the column rule\u{1}\u{1}\u{1}",
        "-webkit-column-rule-style\u{1}Sets the style of the rule between columns of an element.\u{1}\u{1}\u{1}",
        "-webkit-column-rule-width\u{1}Sets the width of the rule between columns. Negative values are not allowed.\u{1}\u{1}\u{1}",
        "-webkit-columns\u{1}A shorthand property which sets both 'column-width' and 'column-count'.\u{1}auto\u{1}\u{1}",
        "-webkit-column-span\u{1}Describes the page/column break behavior after the generated box.\u{1}all none\u{1}\u{1}",
