        "appearance\u{1}Changes the appearance of buttons and other controls to resemble native controls.\u{1}\u{1}none | auto | <compat-auto> | <compat-special>\u{1}",
        "aspect-ratio\u{1}The aspect-ratio CSS property sets a preferred aspect ratio for the box, which will be used in the calculation of auto sizes and some other layout functions.\u{1}\u{1}auto || <ratio>\u{1}",
        "backdrop-filter\u{1}The backdrop-filter CSS property lets you apply graphical effects such as blurring or color shifting to the area behind an element.\u{1}\u{1}none | <filter-value-list>\u{1}",
        "baseline-shift\u{1}Allows repositioning of the dominant-baseline relative to the dominant-baseline of the parent text content element. The shifted object might be a sub- or superscript.\u{1}\u{1}<length-percentage> | sub | super | baseline\u{1}",
        "baseline-source\u{1}\u{1}auto first last\u{1}auto | first | last\u{1}",
        "border-block\u{1}The border-block CSS property is a shorthand property for setting the individual logical block border property values in a single place in the style sheet.\u{1}\u{1}<'border-block-start'>\u{1}",
        "border-block-color\u{1}The border-block-color CSS property defines the color of the logical block borders of an element, which maps to a physical border color depending on the element's writing mode, directionality, and text orientation.\u{1}\u{1}<'border-top-color'>{1,2}\u{1}",
        "border-block-style\u{1}The border-block-style CSS property defines the style of the logical block borders of an element, which maps to a physical border style depending on the element's writing mode, directionality, and text orientation.\u{1}\u{1}<'border-top-style'>{1,2}\u{1}",
