        "border-end-end-radius\u{1}The border-end-end-radius CSS property defines a logical border radius on an element, which maps to a physical border radius that depends on on the element's writing-mode, direction, and text-orientation.\u{1}\u{1}<'border-top-left-radius'>\u{1}",
        "border-end-start-radius\u{1}The border-end-start-radius CSS property defines a logical border radius on an element, which maps to a physical border radius depending on the element's writing-mode, direction, and text-orientation.\u{1}\u{1}<'border-top-left-radius'>\u{1}",
        "border-inline\u{1}The border-inline CSS property is a shorthand property for setting the individual logical inline border property values in a single place in the style sheet.\u{1}\u{1}<'border-block-start'>\u{1}",
        "border-inline-color\u{1}The border-inline-color CSS property defines the color of the logical inline borders of an element, which maps to a physical border color depending on the element's writing mode, directionality, and text orientation.\u{1}\u{1}<'border-top-color'>{1,2}\u{1}",
        "border-inline-style\u{1}The border-inline-style CSS property defines the style of the logical inline borders of an element, which maps to a physical border style depending on the element's writing mode, directionality, and text orientation.\u{1}\u{1}<'border-top-style'>{1,2}\u{1}",
        "border-inline-width\u{1}The border-inline-width CSS property defines the width of the logical inline borders of an element, which maps to a physical border width depending on the element's writing mode, directionality, and text orientation.\u{1}\u{1}<'border-top-width'>{1,2}\u{1}",
        "border-start-end-radius\u{1}The border-start-end-radius CSS property defines a logical border radius on an element, which maps to a physical border radius depending on the element's writing-mode, direction, and text-orientation.\u{1}\u{1}<'border-top-left-radius'>\u{1}",
        "border-start-start-radius\u{1}The border-start-start-radius CSS property defines a logical border radius on an element, which maps to a physical border radius that depends on the element's writing-mode, direction, and text-orientation.\u{1}\u{1}<'border-top-left-radius'>\u{1}",
        "box-align\u{1}The box-align CSS property specifies how an element aligns its contents across its layout in a perpendicular direction. The effect of the property is only visible if there is extra space in the box.\u{1}start center end baseline stretch\u{1}start | center | end | baseline | stretch\u{1}x",
        "box-direction\u{1}The box-direction CSS property specifies whether a box lays out its contents normally (from the top or left edge), or in reverse (from the bottom or right edge).\u{1}normal reverse inherit\u{1}normal | reverse | inherit\u{1}x",
        "box-flex\u{1}The -moz-box-flex and -webkit-box-flex CSS properties specify how a -moz-box or -webkit-box grows to fill the box that contains it, in the direction of the containing box's layout.\u{1}\u{1}<number>\u{1}x",
        "box-flex-group\u{1}The box-flex-group CSS property assigns the flexbox's child elements to a flex group.\u{1}\u{1}<integer>\u{1}x",
        "box-lines\u{1}The box-lines CSS property determines whether the box may have a single or multiple lines (rows for horizontally oriented boxes, columns for vertically oriented boxes).\u{1}single multiple\u{1}single | multiple\u{1}x",
        "box-ordinal-group\u{1}The box-ordinal-group CSS property assigns the flexbox's child elements to an ordinal group.\u{1}\u{1}<integer>\u{1}x",
        "box-orient\u{1}The box-orient CSS property specifies whether an element lays out its contents horizontally or vertically.\u{1}horizontal vertical inline-axis block-axis inherit\u{1}horizontal | vertical | inline-axis | block-axis | inherit\u{1}x",
        "box-pack\u{1}The -moz-box-pack and -webkit-box-pack CSS properties specify how a -moz-box or -webkit-box packs its contents in the direction of its layout. The effect of this is only visible if there is extra space in the box.\u{1}start center end justify\u{1}start | center | end | justify\u{1}x",
        "caret\u{1}Shorthand for setting caret-color and caret-shape.\u{1}\u{1}<'caret-color'> || <'caret-animation'> || <'caret-shape'>\u{1}",
        "caret-animation\u{1}\u{1}auto manual\u{1}auto | manual\u{1}",
        "caret-shape\u{1}Specifies the desired shape of the text insertion caret.\u{1}auto bar block underscore\u{1}auto | bar | block | underscore\u{1}",
        "color-scheme\u{1}The color-scheme CSS property allows an element to indicate which color schemes it can comfortably be rendered in.\u{1}\u{1}normal | [ light | dark | <custom-ident> ]+ && only?\u{1}",
        "column-height\u{1}\u{1}\u{1}auto | <length [0,\u{221e}]>\u{1}",
