        "counter-set\u{1}The counter-set CSS property sets a CSS counter to a given value. It manipulates the value of existing counters, and will only create new counters if there isn't already a counter of the given name on the element.\u{1}\u{1}[ <counter-name> <integer>? ]+ | none\u{1}",
