        "object-view-box\u{1}Defines a rectangle as a viewable area (viewbox) within a replaced element, enabling the content of the replaced element to be zoomed or panned.\u{1}\u{1}none | <basic-shape-rect>\u{1}",
        "offset\u{1}The offset CSS property is a shorthand property for animating an element along a defined path.\u{1}\u{1}[ <'offset-position'>? [ <'offset-path'> [ <'offset-distance'> || <'offset-rotate'> ]? ]? ]! [ / <'offset-anchor'> ]?\u{1}",
        "offset-anchor\u{1}Defines an anchor point of the box positioned along the path. The anchor point specifies the point of the box which is to be considered as the point that is moved along the path.\u{1}\u{1}auto | <position>\u{1}",
        "offset-distance\u{1}The offset-distance CSS property specifies a position along an offset-path.\u{1}\u{1}<length-percentage>\u{1}",
        "offset-path\u{1}The offset-path CSS property specifies the offset path where the element gets positioned. The exact element\u{2019}s position on the offset path is determined by the offset-distance property.\u{1}\u{1}none | <offset-path> || <coord-box>\u{1}",
        "offset-position\u{1}Specifies the initial position of the offset path. If position is specified with static, offset-position would be ignored.\u{1}\u{1}normal | auto | <position>\u{1}",
