        "position-try\u{1}This shorthand sets both position-try-options and position-try-order. If <'position-try-order'> is omitted, it\u{2019}s set to the property\u{2019}s initial value.\u{1}\u{1}<'position-try-order'>? <'position-try-fallbacks'>\u{1}",
        "position-try-fallbacks\u{1}The position-try-fallbacks CSS property enables you to specify a list of one or more alternative position try fallback options for anchor-positioned elements to be placed relative to their associated anchor elements.\u{1}\u{1}none | [ [<dashed-ident> || <try-tactic>] | <'position-area'> ]#\u{1}",
        "position-try-order\u{1}This property specifies the order in which the position options list will be tried.\u{1}\u{1}normal | <try-size>\u{1}",
        "position-visibility\u{1}There are times when an element\u{2019}s anchors are not appropriate for positioning the element with, and it would be better to simply not display the element at all.\u{1}\u{1}always | [ anchors-valid || anchors-visible || no-overflow ]\u{1}",
        "print-color-adjust\u{1}Defines what optimization the user agent is allowed to do when adjusting the appearance for an output device.\u{1}economy exact\u{1}economy | exact\u{1}",
        "r\u{1}The r CSS property defines the radius of a circle. It can only be used with the SVG circle element. If present, it overrides the circle's r attribute.\u{1}\u{1}<length> | <percentage>\u{1}",
        "reading-flow\u{1}\u{1}normal source-order flex-visual flex-flow grid-rows grid-columns grid-order\u{1}normal | source-order | flex-visual | flex-flow | grid-rows | grid-columns | grid-order\u{1}",
        "reading-order\u{1}\u{1}\u{1}<integer>\u{1}",
        "rotate\u{1}The rotate CSS property allows you to specify rotation transforms individually and independently of the transform property.\u{1}\u{1}none | <angle> | [ x | y | z | <number>{3} ] && <angle>\u{1}",
        "row-gap\u{1}The row-gap CSS property specifies the gutter between grid rows.\u{1}\u{1}normal | <length-percentage>\u{1}",
        "ruby-merge\u{1}This property controls how ruby annotation boxes should be rendered when there are more than one in a ruby container box: whether each pair should be kept separate, the annotations should be collapsed and rendered as a group, or...\u{1}separate collapse auto\u{1}separate | collapse | auto\u{1}",
        "rx\u{1}The rx CSS property defines the x-axis, or horizontal, radius of an SVG ellipse and the horizontal curve of the corners of an SVG rect rectangle. If present, it overrides the shape's rx attribute.\u{1}\u{1}<length> | <percentage>\u{1}",
        "ry\u{1}The ry CSS property defines the y-axis, or vertical, radius of an SVG ellipse and the vertical curve of the corners of an SVG rect rectangle. If present, it overrides the shape's ry attribute.\u{1}\u{1}<length> | <percentage>\u{1}",
