        "button\u{1}The button element represents a button labeled by its contents.\u{1}autofocus\u{3}This Boolean attribute lets you specify that the button should have input focus when the page loads, unless the user overrides it, for example by typing in a different control.\u{3}\u{2}disabled\u{3}This Boolean attribute indicates that the user cannot interact with the button. If this attribute is not specified, the button inherits its setting from the containing element, for example <fieldset>...\u{3}\u{2}form\u{3}The form element that the button is associated with (its form owner). The value of the attribute must be the id attribute of a <form> element in the same document.\u{3}\u{2}formaction\u{3}The URI of a program that processes the information submitted by the button. If specified, it overrides the action attribute of the button's form owner.\u{3}\u{2}formenctype\u{3}If the button is a submit button, this attribute specifies the type of content that is used to submit the form to the server.\u{3}application/x-www-form-urlencoded multipart/form-data text/plain\u{2}formmethod\u{3}If the button is a submit button, this attribute specifies the HTTP method that the browser uses to submit the form.\u{3}get post\u{2}formnovalidate\u{3}If the button is a submit button, this Boolean attribute specifies that the form is not to be validated when it is submitted.\u{3}\u{2}formtarget\u{3}If the button is a submit button, this attribute is a name or keyword indicating where to display the response that is received after submitting the form.\u{3}\u{2}name\u{3}The name of the button, which is submitted with the form data.\u{3}\u{2}popovertarget\u{3}Turns the button into a popover control button; takes the ID of the popover element to control as its value.\u{3}\u{2}popovertargetaction\u{3}Specifies the action to be performed on a popover element being controlled by the button.\u{3}\u{2}type\u{3}The type of the button. Possible values are: submit: The button submits the form d